 See https://hankweave.dev/reference/configuration for documentation.\",\n    50→  },\n    51→  {\n    52→    zodSchema: runtimeConfigSchema,\n    53→    outputFile: \"hankweave.schema.json\",\n    54→    title: \"Hankweave Runtime Configuration\",\n    55→    description:\n    56→      \"Schema for hankweave.json - runtime settings for the Hankweave server. See https://hankweave.dev/reference/configuration for documentation.\",\n    57→  },\n    58→  {\n    59→    zodSchema: sentinelConfigSchema,\n    60→    outputFile: \"sentinel.schema.json\",\n    61→    title: \"Hankweave Sentinel Configuration\",\n    62→    description:\n    63→      \"Schema for sentinel configuration files - parallel observation agents. Note: Some runtime validations cannot be expressed in JSON Schema. See https://hankweave.dev/reference/sentinel-config for documentation.\",\n    64→  },\n    65→];\n    66→\n    67→async function generateSchemas() {\n    68→  console.log(\"Generating JSON schemas...\\n\");\n    69→\n    70→  // Ensure package schemas directory exists (required)\n    71→  if (!fs.existsSync(SCHEMA_DIR)) {\n    72→    fs.mkdirSync(SCHEMA_DIR, { recursive: true });\n    73→  }\n    74→\n    75→  // Check if docs directory exists (optional - only used if hosting schemas on hankweave.dev)\n    76→  const docsAvailable = fs.existsSync(path.dirname(DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR));\n    77→  if (docsAvailable && !fs.existsSync(DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR)) {\n    78→    fs.mkdirSync(DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR, { recursive: true });\n    79→  }\n    80→\n    81→  for (const config of schemas) {\n    82→    console.log(`Generating ${config.outputFile}...`);\n    83→\n    84→    // @ts-ignore - zodToJsonSchema has excessively deep types\n    85→    const jsonSchema: Record<string, unknown> = zodToJsonSchema(config.zodSchema, {\n    86→      name: config.title.replace(/\\s+/g, \"\"),\n    87→      target: \"jsonSchema7\", // Draft-07 for VS Code compatibility\n    88→      $refStrategy: \"none\", // Inline all definitions